+ * header, tracks the per-point last TCP seq, and logs ONLY when seq goes
+ * backwards (a reorder/retransmit as seen at this point). Reorder-only logging =
+ * no per-packet flood. Two call sites bracket the rmnet deaggr/demux:
+ *   ING = ingress entry (order as IPA delivered the QMAP buffer)
+ *   DLV = rmnet_deliver_skb (clean IP, post-deaggr, just before gro_cells)
+ * ING reordered -> IPA/modem; ING ok & DLV reordered -> rmnet deaggr; both ok but
+ * TCP still reordered -> gro_cells. Assumes a single TCP flow under test.
